# Every pattern here is written `**/x` rather than `x`, because the same directory now appears
# once per workspace as well as at the root, and a root-anchored pattern would let the copy
# inside `packages/` through.

# The image installs its own from the lockfile, and this one was installed on the host, quite
# possibly for another platform — the image is linux/amd64, the host often is not.
**/node_modules/

# Build output and test artifacts: produced inside the image, and copying them in only makes
# "which copy is this" a question with two answers.
**/dist/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/

# Local state that has no business in a test image.
.git/
# Wayfinding, and where the screen sweep leaves its pictures. The sweep writes about 10 MB into
# `.scratch/shots/` on every run, and inside the build context that is 10 MB of churn which
# invalidates `COPY . .` — so the next sweep would rebuild frond before it could start.
.scratch/
**/.wrangler/
**/public/fixtures/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
